      "message": "Before deleting the fingerprint boards and shared code, please:\n\n* Create a CL that updates the [documentation on creating a fingerprint firmware release](http://shortn/_w7pcBoTjDR).\n* Address [this comment](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/7122379/comments/9cd0a895_3d5c689d).\n* Point the [fingerprint documentation](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/docs/sitemap.md#fingerprint-mcu-fpmcu) in the legacy repo to the docs in `main`.\n* Set up a session for the FP team to walk everyone else through what is changing and where to find everything.\n\nI would also suggest splitting this into two CLs:\n\n* One that deletes everything except what is needed to build `bloonchipper` and `helipilot`.\n* A second one that then deletes the `bloonchipper` and `helipilot` code.\n\nThat way you can make forward progress on deleting code without our approval and have an easy way to revert only the fingerprint-related code if there are issues that come up after deleting it.\n\nAdding @patrykd@google.com and @dabros@google.com in case they have any other requests.",
